Web Development
1. Difference between Frontend, Backend and Full-Stack Development
Frontend Development: Frontend is the part of a website that users can see and interact with. Technologies include HTML, CSS, JavaScript and React. Example: On an online shopping website, product images, buttons, menus and the shopping cart interface are frontend.
Backend Development: Backend is the server-side part of a website. It handles business logic, databases, authentication and requests from the frontend. Technologies include Java, Python, Node.js and PHP. Example: When a user logs in, the backend checks the username and password from the database.
Full-Stack Development: Full-stack development involves working on both frontend and backend of an application. Example: A full-stack developer can create the shopping website interface, develop its server-side logic and connect it to the database.
