8. Difference Between Static and Dynamic Websites
Static Website: A static website displays fixed content. The content generally remains the same unless the developer manually changes the files. Example: A portfolio website.
Dynamic Website: A dynamic website generates or changes content based on user interaction, database information or other conditions. Example: Amazon or an online banking website.
Static websites are generally simpler and faster to develop, while dynamic websites often require server-side processing and databases.
9. Five Web Browsers and Their Rendering Engines
1. Google Chrome – Blink
2. Microsoft Edge – Blink
3. Mozilla Firefox – Gecko
4. Apple Safari – WebKit
5. Opera – Blink
Rendering engines interpret HTML, CSS and other webpage resources and convert them into the visual webpage displayed by the browser.
